        ],
        "dependency_level": 4,
        "proof_strategy": "direct",
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "literature-derived",
          "proof": "ai-generated"
        },
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "Stefan Friedl, Knot Theory, §5.3, proof of the Wirtinger Presentation Proposition",
              "url": "https://friedl.app.uni-regensburg.de/papers/2024_knot-theory-final.pdf",
              "locator": "Claim 1a and the local crossing charts, printed pp. 69–70, PDF pp. 70–71"
            },
            {
              "title": "Cole Charbonneau, Computing the Wirtinger Presentation of a Knot Group from a Knot Diagram",
              "url": "https://site.uvm.edu/cmcharbo/files/2021/12/knot-group-1.pdf",
              "locator": "§§2–3, local meridian-conjugacy construction; knot case only"
            }
          ]
        },
        "statement": "At an oriented crossing let $o$ be the over-strand. Orient the projection plane\nby the rule that $(v_1,v_2)$ is a positive basis exactly when the ordered triple\n$(n,v_1,v_2)$ is positive in the ambient three-space, where $n$ is the viewing\nnormal. Let $n_o$ be the positive in-plane normal characterized by the condition\nthat $(v_o,n_o)$ is positive in this plane. Call the under-side from\nwhich $n_o$ points the source $s$, and the side toward which it points the\ntarget $t$. Use a common basepoint above the diagram and paths in the upper\ncollar to the positive meridians $m_o,m_s,m_t$. Then\n$$m_t=m_o^{-1}m_sm_o.$$\nEquivalently, the crossing relator is\n$m_o^{-1}m_sm_om_t^{-1}=1$. Reversing the direction of the under-strand\ndoes not change the side-based equation.",
